data: {"type": "assistant_msg", "ts": "2026-08-06T12:23:43.965686+00:00", "content": "Based on the live telemetry for **ce_branch24**, here are the observed faults formatted as a Mermaid diagram:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n    %% Device node\n    CE24[\"ce_branch24\\n(172.20.20.160)\"]\n    \n    %% Physical interfaces\n    ETH0[\"eth0\\n(index 2)\"]\n    ETH1[\"eth1\\n(index 515)\"]\n    ETH2[\"eth2\\n(index 744)\"]\n    ETH3[\"eth3\\n(index 531)\"]\n    ETH4[\"eth4\\n(index 754)\"]\n    \n    %% VRFs & Tunnel\n    VRF_CORP[\"vrf_CORP\"]\n    VRF_VOICE[\"vrf_VOICE\"]\n    WG0[\"wg0 (WireGuard)\"]\n    \n    %% SD-WAN Tunnels\n    TUN_HUB1[\"ce_branch24-ce_hub1\"]\n    TUN_HUB2[\"ce_branch24-ce_hub2\"]\n    TUN_HUB3[\"ce_branch24-ce_hub3\"]\n    TUN_HUB4[\"ce_branch24-ce_hub4\"]\n    TUN_HUB5[\"ce_branch24-ce_hub5\"]\n    TUN_HUB6[\"ce_branch24-ce_hub6\"]\n    \n    %% Connections\n    CE24 --> ETH0\n    CE24 --> ETH1\n    CE24 --> ETH2\n    CE24 --> ETH3\n    CE24 --> ETH4\n    CE24 --> VRF_CORP\n    CE24 --> VRF_VOICE\n    CE24 --> WG0\n    \n    WG0 --> TUN_HUB1\n    WG0 --> TUN_HUB2\n    WG0 --> TUN_HUB3\n    WG0 --> TUN_HUB4\n    WG0 --> TUN_HUB5\n    WG0 --> TUN_HUB6\n    \n    %% Fault annotations (red styling)\n    classDef fault fill:#ffcccc,stroke:#cc0000,stroke-width:2px;\n    classDef warn fill:#fff3cc,stroke:#cc8800,stroke-width:2px;\n    classDef ok fill:#ccffcc,stroke:#006600;\n    \n    %% eth0 faults\n    FAULT_ETH0_DROPS[\"\u26a0 Queue Drops: 92\\n[metrics:6]\"]\n    FAULT_ETH0_DISCARDS[\"\u26a0 In Discards: 1,877\\n[metrics:26]\"]\n    ETH0 -.-> FAULT_ETH0_DROPS\n    ETH0 -.-> FAULT_ETH0_DISCARDS\n    \n    %% eth1 minor fault\n    FAULT_ETH1_DROPS[\"\u26a0 Queue Drops: 2\\n[metrics:7]\"]\n    ETH1 -.-> FAULT_ETH1_DROPS\n    \n    %% Tunnel faults\n    FAULT_HUB3_JITTER[\"\ud83d\udd34 HIGH JITTER: 79.27 ms\\n[metrics:2]\"]\n    FAULT_HUB3_LATENCY[\"\ud83d\udd34 HIGH LATENCY: 108.94 ms\\n[metrics:8]\"]\n    FAULT_HUB2_REKEYS[\"\ud83d\udd34 REKEYS: 26\\n[metrics:1]\"]\n    FAULT_HUB3_REKEYS[\"\ud83d\udd34 REKEYS: 26\\n[metrics:2]\"]\n    FAULT_HUB5_LOSS[\"\u26a0 Loss: 0.19%\\n[metrics:16]\"]\n    \n    TUN_HUB3 -.-> FAULT_HUB3_JITTER\n    TUN_HUB3 -.-> FAULT_HUB3_LATENCY\n    TUN_HUB2 -.-> FAULT_HUB2_REKEYS\n    TUN_HUB3 -.-> FAULT_HUB3_REKEYS\n    TUN_HUB5 -.-> FAULT_HUB5_LOSS\n    \n    %% VRF zero egress (informational)\n    INFO_VRF_CORP[\"\u2139 0 Out Octets (CORP)\\n[metrics:23]\"]\n    INFO_VRF_VOICE[\"\u2139 0 Out Octets (VOICE)\\n[metrics:24]\"]\n    VRF_CORP -.-> INFO_VRF_CORP\n    VRF_VOICE -.-> INFO_VRF_VOICE\n    \n    class FAULT_ETH0_DROPS,FAULT_ETH0_DISCARDS,FAULT_HUB3_JITTER,FAULT_HUB3_LATENCY,FAULT_HUB2_REKEYS,FAULT_HUB3_REKEYS fault;\n    class FAULT_ETH1_DROPS,FAULT_HUB5_LOSS warn;\n    class INFO_VRF_CORP,INFO_VRF_VOICE ok;\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Faults (with citations)\n\n| Component | Fault | Severity | Evidence |\n|-----------|-------|----------|----------|\n| **eth0** | 92 queue drops | \u26a0 Warning | [metrics:6] |\n| **eth0** | 1,877 inbound discards | \u26a0 Warning | [metrics:26] |\n| **eth1** | 2 queue drops | \u26a0 Minor | [metrics:7] |\n| **Tunnel \u2192 ce_hub3** | Jitter 79.27 ms (vs ~4\u20139 ms others) | \ud83d\udd34 Critical | [metrics:2] |\n| **Tunnel \u2192 ce_hub3** | Latency 108.94 ms (vs ~64\u201375 ms others) | \ud83d\udd34 Critical | [metrics:8] |\n| **Tunnel \u2192 ce_hub2** | 26 rekeys (high vs 5\u20136 on others) | \ud83d\udd34 Critical | [metrics:1] (rekey query) |\n| **Tunnel \u2192 ce_hub3** | 26 rekeys (high vs 5\u20136 on others) | \ud83d\udd34 Critical | [metrics:2] (rekey query) |\n| **Tunnel \u2192 ce_hub5** | Loss 0.19% (highest of the set) | \u26a0 Warning | [metrics:16] |\n| **vrf_CORP / vrf_VOICE** | Zero egress traffic | \u2139 Informational | [metrics:23], [metrics:24] |\n\nThe most actionable issues are the **ce_hub3 tunnel degradation** (jitter + latency + rekeys) and **ce_hub2 excessive rekeys**, suggesting path instability or MTU/keepalive mismatch on those two hub links. The eth0 discards/drops warrant a counter-increment rate check to see if they're ongoing."}

